WEBVTT

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.920
So, since the event is so close,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.590
Summer has asked us
to pick someone to sub in.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.390
But why her, ma'am?

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:22.850
Unfortunately for you
second-years in the 99th class,

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.020
since this is our centennial year,
we wanted someone from the 100th class.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.360
We could've simply picked
the top student in the grade,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.070
but decided to try something
a little different.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.990
All right,

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.660
Sarasa Watanabe-<i>san</i>,
we'll be counting on you!

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.500
Wait... what?

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.760
The other girls weren't too thrilled
about her getting picked...

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.560
"A Once-in-a-Century Autumn"

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.850
"A Once-in-a-Century Autumn"
I'm cool with it, but...

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.480
Why does Sarasa get
<i>all </i>the cool opportunities?

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.280
Normally they'd go by grades.
That would mean you, Sawa.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.650
The Superiors have made their decision.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.280
And remember, there's no such thing
as normal in our world.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.910
This better not make
the second-years bully us even harder.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:54.340
Oh, Watanabe-<i>san</i>! Good morning!

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.130
Here I thought you'd be too busy prepping
for the festival to clean. Good for you!

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.590
Good morning, Hijiri-<i>senpai</i>!

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.090
Are you heading off to help clean, too?

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.350
Yeah, you know.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.600
Boy, the 100th class is so lucky!

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.940
Have you met with
the Summer Troupe participants yet?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.070
Yeah! We had one meeting for everyone
participating in the relay race.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.900
Their top star, Reo Shiina, was there,

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.860
and so was Aika Shion, and Jou Kisaragi...

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.320
Did they say anything to you?

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.910
Umm...

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.990
"Whoa, you're so tall!"

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:30.540
You sure are known for your height,
aren't you, Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.420
You're just like the birdlime tree,
only special because of its height.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:39.300
Personally, I would have
picked Narata-<i>san</i>,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.220
since people would <i>love </i>seeing her out on
stage, and she'd make quite the splash.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:46.300
But I must concede that us students
must let the stars shine,

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.430
so do your best <i>not </i>to stand out!

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.350
Okay! I'll try super duper hard!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.690
No. You don't get it at all, do you?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:55.860
Huh?!

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.280
You shouldn't try hard.
In fact, don't try at all!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.240
The only people who should stand out
are the actual members of the Troupe!

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.990
You can't help your height, but turn
your big personality all the way off!

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.450
Make it as if you're not even there!
Become nothingness itself!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.870
I only barely noticed it,
but I could tell...

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.750
"AI NARATA"
"SARASA WATANABE"

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.750
I only barely noticed it,
but I could tell...

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:15.630
"AI NARATA"
"SARASA WATANABE"

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:15.630
Sarasa had taken
those words far too literally.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.880
Sarasa had taken
those words far too literally.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.300
Nothing... Become nothingness...

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:29.470
Someone wise once said,
"Don't think, feel."

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:34.640
When you were in JPX, were you
ever nervous out on stage, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.100
Are you nervous?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.690
Yeah.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.520
Whoa.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.530
I got used to people
staring at me from an early age.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.780
When I started disliking the attention,

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.580
I learned how to filter it out entirely.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.420
I hope I can learn how to do that
before the Sports Festival.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.710
You know, I don't think that's
the best approach.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:04.220
I realized something during that class
on <i>Romeo and Juliet </i>this summer,

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:07.390
when I was watching Andou-<i>sensei</i>'s
reaction to our performance.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:12.850
It's not enough to just pretend you're
paying attention to the audience.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:18.810
Ignoring the audience entirely
is the wrong choice, too.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.190
You have to consider what they're
looking for, what they want to see,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:27.240
and be conscious of that
while you're up on stage.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.080
What the audience wants to see?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:34.500
I don't think anyone
wants to see <i>me </i>out there!

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.250
That didn't cheer her up at all...

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.090
Soon, the day of the Festival was here.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.010
The Spring Troupe has arrived!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.890
Summer's going for their streak!

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.100
The Autumn Troupe's going for the gold!

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.890
Winter's gonna give it our all!

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:56.180
The Superior-Student team is here!

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.850
The limiter that restrains
the Kouka fans' burning passion...

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.770
"Hakusen Grand Hall"

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.770
The limiter that restrains
the Kouka fans' burning passion...

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.150
"Hakusen Grand Hall"

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.150
...gets to be turned off
only once every ten years...

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.240
...here at the Kouka
Grand Sports Festival.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.530
It's been a long decade,
but the moment is finally here!

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.450
Without further ado,
here come our combatants!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.330
From the Spring Troupe, Ryuu Asahina!

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.540
From the Summer Troupe, Reo Shiina!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.380
From the Autumn Troupe, Keito Mitsuki!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.220
From the Winter Troupe, Sei Satomi!

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.640
Last but not least,
the Superior-Student team!

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:38.890
Now, our Troupe representatives will lead
the combatants in the honor pledge!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.650
Today, we pledge...

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.940
To uphold the Kouka spirit!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.820
To compete gallantly,
fairly, and beautifully!

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.610
To represent our Troupes
with all that we have!

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.700
This we solemnly swear!

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.200
"Spring Troupe"

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.450
"Sei-<i>sama</i>"

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.330
The Troupe entrance ceremony was so cool!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.290
Yeah! And everyone
really liked our dance, too!

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.000
That was better than
all our rehearsals, too, yeah?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.050
--Yeah!
--Watanabe-<i>san</i>,

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:10.220
you messed up during
the second verse's choreo, I think.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.720
S-Sorry!

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:14.800
Could you prep the flags
for the next event?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.310
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.810
Oh, I'll come hel--

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:22.690
That's okay! Besides, only the
second-years can help out with events.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.940
And of those second-years, only those
who are most capable get the honor.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.530
And that's determined by grades!

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.820
If I recall, Watanabe-<i>san</i>,
your grades aren't--

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:32.660
Hijiri!

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.370
Oop, I'd better go!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.750
Okay, Hijiri,

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.620
you seriously need to stop
messing with Sarasa Watanabe.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.000
You're stunting her growth.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:48.050
I'm not messing with her.
I'm just a little jealous.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:50.380
What the hell?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:55.350
She stands out, and everyone
expects great things from her.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:59.140
Not only that, but she's also best friends
with my darling Naracchi.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:02.520
What? God, Hijiri, you're such--

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.350
A bitch?

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:08.780
But I'm not <i>trying </i>to be a bitch,
so I've got nothing to worry about!

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.320
Anyways, Risa, why are you
wasting time scolding me,

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.450
when you should probably be
comforting Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.500
Look how lovely our Troupes are
as they take the field!

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.000
The Giant Ball Roll!

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.750
Their path will lead them down
the silver bridge to the finish line...

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:31.090
...in the 75-meter race!

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.050
What a magnificent, jaunty line dance!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.430
The Dancing Ball Toss!

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:43.230
I tell you, you'd only see sports like
these right here with the Kouka troupe!

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:43.730
"Halftime Scores"

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:43.730
I tell you, you'd only see sports like
these right here with the Kouka troupe!

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.730
"Halftime Scores"

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.730
Let's see what
our scores are at halftime:

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.060
In first place, the Summer Troupe,
with 83 points!

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.730
"FIRST: SUMMER"

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.730
In first place, the Summer Troupe,
with 83 points!

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:51.820
"FIRST: SUMMER"

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:51.820
Coming in second is
Spring with 67 points!

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.070
"FIRST: SUMMER"
"SECOND: SPRING"

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.070
Coming in second is
Spring with 67 points!

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.320
Next up: the spirited cheer-off!

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.120
First up, we have
the Superior-Student team!

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.910
We will be performing the school song,

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:06.120
"Amongst the Cherry Blossoms in the Wind"!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:03.890
Wonderful! What a delightful performance.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.560
But she didn't seem to be
her usual, energetic self.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:11.730
Oh my, Takei isn't here.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.690
Guess I've got no choice.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.440
Narata-<i>san</i>, will you come help me?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.780
Sure.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.660
Look, it's Naracchi!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.870
She's so cute!

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.790
The second-year girl
with her is cute, too!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.870
Hijiri, you conniving little bitch.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.330
Naracchi is hardly fazed.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.130
Hey, Sarasa, are you okay?

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.920
You didn't mess up at all. You're fine.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.550
You're wrong.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:40.010
I did something even worse
than messing up.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.680
I was so scared of messing up...

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.480
...that I didn't even <i>play </i>my recorder!

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:49.890
Excuse me, Ichijou-<i>san</i>!

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.770
Watanabe-<i>san</i>'s feeling a little off.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.690
Oh, dear! Want to take a little break?

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:59.820
Thank you, ma'am. We'll be back in ten.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.870
Okay, what the hell is up?
You've been acting weird this whole time!

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.790
It's just...

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:09.660
I'm nervous and putting so much pressure
on myself, and I don't know what to do...

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.920
What? <i>You're </i>nervous?!

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.460
What's got you so nervous, huh?

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:21.680
I-I'm totally fine playing a role,
like Lady Oscar, in front of other people,

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.140
but today, I have to be myself.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.270
It feels like I'm going out
on stage butt-naked!

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:34.980
I don't know how to not stand out
and outshine the top stars.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:39.280
I keep thinking how Ai-<i>chan </i>or Hijiri-<i>senpai</i>
would've been way better choices.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.320
Or you, Risa-<i>senpai</i>! You're pretty
and have a great figure,

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.780
--so you'd make a way better sub than--
--Cut the crap already!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.700
The Superiors picked you!

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.000
Remember what you said to me before?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.580
You were lucky enough to get in here,
so you weren't going to give up!

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.420
You're going to play Lady Oscar, right?!

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:58.670
You were picked for whatever reason,
and sure, that might piss people off!

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:01.880
But if you give up now,
you'll piss them off even more!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:05.600
That's just what it means
to put yourself out there!

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:10.180
So you can't get out of this.
You have to see this through to the end!

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.600
She's right.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.520
And if you're scared of putting
your real self out there, do this.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.360
Take on the role of a ridiculously-tall
first-year student at the Kouka school

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:26.280
who's been asked to sub in for
the Sports Festival relay race.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.740
That's how we do it, too.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:34.750
We're always playing the 'role' of
our troupe's top star, even off stage.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:42.300
Right, so, someone just shoved
this bouquet into my hand,

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:46.180
and told me to give it to
"the tall first-year with pigtails."

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:49.720
I didn't want to give them
to you <i>here</i>, obviously.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:54.060
And I have no idea how he got in.
Only staff are supposed to be back here.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:59.610
But he told me to tell you "good luck in
the race, from your fan of the red rose."

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:03.030
What a weirdo. Freaked me out, honestly.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.110
I should get back to my seat.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:10.240
Risa-<i>senpai</i>, Satomi-<i>san</i>,
thank you both so much!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.870
You a second-year?

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.670
Oh, yes!

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:18.670
What's your name?

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:20.210
Risa Nakayama, ma'am!

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.550
Okay.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.630
C'mon, you should go, too.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:25.470
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:31.560
Aww, man. I wish I could've
watched Sarasa's relay race.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.190
You snooped through my phone again?!

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.900
Too bad. We've gotta
get back to Minami-za.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:44.610
You always go overboard. Could you
not embarrass me for once?

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:47.320
Oh, Akiya, you'll get there one day.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.950
Besides, actors have to forget
what shame is to do their job right!

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.840
Sarasa, you went with Nakayama-<i>senpai</i>,
right? Was everything okay?

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.340
Yep! She gave me a pep talk!

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:11.180
The scary kind?

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:15.430
Not at all! She gave me some great advice.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:18.980
They picked me,
so there's no running away now.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:22.730
That's just what it means
to put yourself out there.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:26.820
Also, our stage is wherever
other people can see us,

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.740
so we have to play the part accordingly.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:36.540
Unfortunately, I don't know what it means
to play the role of myself.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:41.630
I'm already me, so wouldn't playing
the <i>role </i>of me just mean being myself?

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:46.420
But that would mean I'm not acting,
I'm just being me...

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.630
You're making this way too complicated.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:52.100
You don't have to be you as you are now.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.140
You could be the person
you want people to think you are,

00:14:55.140 --> 00:15:00.310
or your ideal self, the person
you've always wanted to be.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.940
My ideal self...

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.450
I've always wanted...

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.740
...E-cups!

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.280
Wait, what?

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:13.490
I want E-cups!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.700
I mean, I heard you the first time!

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:21.790
I've always wanted to put on one of
those tight-fitting anime battle suits,

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:27.380
but they wouldn't look good on me unless
my boobs were big enough to fill it out.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.670
Sure, do that.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.220
Wait, really?!

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.800
What would a girl with E-cups
worry about at a sports festival?

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:37.220
Um, if I usually tried to hide my chest,

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:40.140
it'd be hard to hide them
in a gym uniform.

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:44.150
They'd be heavy when I ran,
and it'd be hard to run fast.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.570
I wouldn't want everyone
looking at them, either.

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:51.740
But you see tons of busty girls in anime
jumping and fighting just fine,

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:55.580
so I've gotta give it my best shot, too!

00:15:55.580 --> 00:16:01.830
That's who E-cup,
16-year-old Sarasa Watanabe is!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.670
It's time for our final event!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.250
Which troupe will clinch victory
and which will taste defeat?!

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:10.260
"Final Event: Troupe Relay Race"

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:10.260
Our final event is
the long-anticipated relay race!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.720
"Runner Introduction"

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.720
Here come your runners!

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:13.550
For Spring Troupe,

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:20.020
Maki Shishido, Fuuta Shiranui, Airi Mashu,
Anna Aki, and Robin Raikou!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:20.850
For Summer Troupe,

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:26.820
Reo Shiina, Aika Shion, Jou Kisaragi,
Rin Enami, Mei Sakura,

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.820
and a special sub-in...

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:33.530
...first-year student Sarasa Watanabe!

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.780
A first-year?

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.320
She's so tall!

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.660
She looks... normal.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.370
No, look!

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.710
She's squeezing her arms into her chest!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:44.540
Like she's trying to hide...

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.290
...her fake big boobs!

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:50.050
Hey, we're both running seventh.

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.550
Go easy on me, mmkay?

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:52.800
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.470
Hey, Sei! Don't mess with our sub!

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.720
Was it that obvious?

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.640
We're not gonna let Winter win this thing!

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:05.980
On your marks, get set...

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.480
And they're off!

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:12.070
The first troupe to
take the lead is Autumn!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.780
Boy, is Autumn fast!

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:17.990
Whoa, Winter's close on her tail!

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:20.700
Autumn takes a tumble...
no, she's back up!

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:21.910
What a recovery!

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:27.130
That competitive drive shows just how hot
the Kouka spirit burns within her!

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:31.630
I can't be so hung-up on my big boobs!

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.760
I've gotta run as fast as I can!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.220
"Fully into her busty role."

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.840
Summer's fast! Too fast!

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.930
Why, she's overtaking Winter!

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:42.100
We're in first?!

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.640
Here we go.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:46.020
Summer and Winter are neck and neck!

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.270
Here!

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:48.270
Got it!

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.980
Sorry I let her get ahead!

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.270
It's okay!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.830
Oh, jeez.

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:09.420
Not her fault. Sei-<i>sama </i>crashed into her.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:15.050
I can't believe this is happening.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:17.840
What should I do now?

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:21.600
Should I stand up and run
to help Summer win?

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:25.270
Or should I apologize and
try to help Satomi-<i>san </i>up?

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:28.600
What's the best option?

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.940
I gotta think... I gotta think!

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:39.990
Ignoring the audience entirely
is the wrong choice, too.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:43.830
You have to consider what they're
looking for, what they want to see,

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.710
and be conscious of that
while you're up on stage.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:50.210
What the audience wants to see...

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.040
They want...

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.670
Ow, ow...

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:56.210
Good, I didn't twist it or anything.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.980
You okay?

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.440
Need a hand?

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:17.360
Thanks!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:21.740
No prob. C'mon!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:23.990
Let's run!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.160
Okay!

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:29.120
After being left in the dust,

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:33.130
Winter and Summer are passing
their batons at the same time!

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.420
Spring takes the win, then Autumn!

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:38.170
The Superior-Student team takes third!

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:43.890
And Summer and Winter's anchors
come across the finish line holding hands!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.060
Thanks.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:57.110
You were right, she is interesting,

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.030
Sensei.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.320
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.030
Did you get hurt? Are you okay?

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:07.330
Your advice saved me!
I wouldn't have made it without it!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:12.500
I don't know why,
but if you say so, then good.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.830
What a memorable centennial.

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:18.960
This Sports Festival was
even more fun than all the others.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.010
I agree.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:24.390
I hope for the 110th, 120th,
and every ten years after that,

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:29.930
a new group of lovely young ladies
will take the baton and pass it down.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:33.140
By the way, why'd you
pick that girl to sub in?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.360
Oh, not for any big reason.

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:39.610
I wanted to reward her for
standing up for her friend earlier.

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:41.570
That, and, well...

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:47.530
She gushed about my performance as Oscar
ten years ago, without knowing it was me.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.160
I couldn't help myself.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.540
Oh, you.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:51.580
"Grand Sports Festival"

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.000
"Grand Sports Festival"

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.000
And now for the final results!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.120
And now for the final results!

00:20:54.120 --> 00:21:00.670
The winners of the Grand Sports Festival
in our centennial year are...

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:02.920
The Spring Troupe!

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.680
Yes!

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:09.060
Spring brings a beautiful storm of
cherry blossoms to our centennial year!

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:14.640
The Spring Troupe and their illustrious
Ryuu Asahina have grasped victory!

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:19.270
Thus concludes our centennial year's
Grand Sports Festival.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:23.780
Thank you all for coming. I hope you
thoroughly enjoyed the show.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:30.120
I'm glad we were able to put our
teamwork and dedication on display,

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:35.330
and make this Sports Festival one
truly worthy of our centennial year.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:41.210
And from all of us in the Kouka troupe,
thank you for your continued support!

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.260
One last round of applause
for our competitors!

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.890
Everything went off without a hitch.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.850
I was so nervous!

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:56.480
I was nervous, too,

00:21:56.480 --> 00:22:02.530
but I got to meet new people
and learn so many new things.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:05.320
The next Sports Festival is in ten years.

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:10.780
We'll have to be fine
Kouka ladies by then!

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:46.960
"Act 11: 4/40"
